2. What is NOT taken from anywhere
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Everything under `app/src/main/kotlin/dev/vantara/spike/` is original
VANTARA code. In particular `FileExtensionLoader.kt` — loading an extension
from a file in app-private storage rather than from an installed package —
was written from the public, documented behaviour of `DexClassLoader`,
`PackageManager.getPackageArchiveInfo` and the Android 14 read-only
requirement for dynamically loaded code.

**No code was taken from TsukiMix** (https://github.com/UsagiApp/TsukiMix).
TsukiMix is licensed **GPL-3.0**, which is copyleft: copying from it would
place all of VANTARA under GPL-3.0. It was read as prior art only, and the
techniques it demonstrates are facts about the DEX format and the Android
platform, not its expression.

**No code was taken from dion-runtime** (https://github.com/bldng1337/dion-runtime).
That repository publishes **no license at all** — neither a LICENSE file,
nor a license field in its manifests, nor a statement in its docs — which
means all rights are reserved and it cannot lawfully be reused.

`ExtensionSignatureVerifier` concepts were informed by Otaku-Reader
(https://github.com/HeartlessVeteran2/Otaku-Reader), Apache License 2.0.


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
3. Extensions themselves are not bundled
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

No Keiyoushi extension binary is committed to this repository. The spike
downloads extension APKs at runtime from the Keiyoushi extension repository
and verifies each one against a pinned SHA-256 before loading it. The
extensions remain the work of their own authors under their own terms.
